hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27546","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Munkadir heard Umaymah bint Ruqayqah say: I pledged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among women, and he dictated to us: in what you are able and capable of. I said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves. I said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge us. He said: I do not shake hands with women; my word to one woman is my word to a hundred women."
"27547","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from Umaymah bint Ruqayqah al-Taymiyyah, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among Muslim women to pledge him. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we come to pledge you upon not associating anything with Allah, not stealing, not committing adultery, not killing our children, not bringing slander we fabricate between our hands and feet, and not disobeying you in good. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In what you are able and obey. She said: We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves; pledge us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Go, I have pledged you; my word to a hundred women is like my word to one woman. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not shake hands with any woman among us."
"27548","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Umaymah bint Ruqayqah, that she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among women pledging him. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we pledge you upon not associating anything with Allah, not stealing, not committing adultery, not bringing slander we fabricate between our hands and feet, and not disobeying you in good. He said: He said: In what you are able and obey. She said: We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves; come, pledge us, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I do not shake hands with women; my word to a hundred women is like my word to one woman."
"27549","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn al-Munkadir, from Umaymah bint Ruqayqah, she said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among women pledging him, and he took upon us what is in the Quran: not to associate anything with Allah - the verse. He said: In what you are able and obey. We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves. We said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not shake hands with us? He said: I do not shake hands with women; my word to one woman is like my word to a hundred women."
"27550","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Umaymah bint Ruqayqah narrate that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I do not shake hands with women; my word to one woman is like my word to a hundred women."
